    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#hugh-capet">Hugh Capet</a> was elected king in 987, it was ruled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#capetian-dynasty">Capetians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#house-of-valois">Valois</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#house-of-bourbon">Bourbons</a> for more than 800 years.</li><li>Its kings grew a small domain around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#paris">Paris</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#europe">Europe</a>'s most populous kingdom through war, marriage, inheritance and law.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#versailles">Versailles</a> made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#france">France</a> the model of European monarchy, but unreformed debt led to the Revolution of 1789.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#estates-general-france">Estates-General</a>, the kingdom's assembly of clergy, nobles and commons, did not meet at all between 1614 and 1789, when its summons opened the Revolution.</p></aside>
    </section>

